IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 3 -- General provisions applying to Acts (ss 9 to 14D).
-- "Passed" and "enacted" are the fact of royal assent (s 15), so an Act's date of assent is the date compared with a date in these sections.
-- The commencement of this Act and of s 13A and s 13B is not stated in the text; where a section turns on it, the fact is an input.

§ `Part 3 -- General provisions applying to Acts`

§§ `s 9 -- Interpretation of Act in relation to Parliament's legislative power`

-- src:38 | (1) An Act is to be interpreted as operating—
-- src:39 | (a) to the full extent of, but not to exceed, Parliament’s legislative power; and
-- src:40 | (b) distributively.
@ref s 9(1) (src:38-40)
GIVEN `the thing is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act is interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but not to exceed, Parliament's legislative power (s 9(1)(a))` IS
    IF `the thing is an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:38 | (1) An Act is to be interpreted as operating—
-- src:39 | (a) to the full extent of, but not to exceed, Parliament’s legislative power; and
-- src:40 | (b) distributively.
@ref s 9(1) (src:38-40)
GIVEN `the thing is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act is interpreted as operating distributively (s 9(1)(b))` IS
    IF `the thing is an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (1A): the declaration is about the legislative power conferred under the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 5 and the
-- Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4, which are not among the sources; whether the power is conferred under them is an input.
-- src:41 | (1A) Without limiting subsection (1)(a), it is declared that subsection applies (and always applied) to the legislative power conferred on Parliament under the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 5 and the Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth), section 4.
@ref s 9(1A) (src:41-41)
