GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration about the Coastal Waters Acts (Cwlth) applies and always applied (s 9(1A))` IS
    IF `the legislative power is conferred under the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 (Cwlth) s 5 or the Coastal Waters (State Title) Act 1980 (Cwlth) s 4` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:42 | (1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply in relation to the substantive criminal law, and the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, under the cooperative scheme as defined under the Crimes at Sea Act 2001, section 3.
@ref s 9(1B) (src:42-42)
GIVEN `it is the substantive criminal law, or the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, under the cooperative scheme defined in the Crimes at Sea Act 2001 s 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration in s 9(1A) applies to the matter (s 9(1B))` IS
    IF `it is the substantive criminal law, or the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, under the cooperative scheme defined in the Crimes at Sea Act 2001 s 3` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): a provision that would be interpreted as exceeding power is "valid to the extent to which it does not exceed power", and the remainder of the Act is not affected.
-- src:43 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a provision of an Act would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding power—
-- src:44 | (a) the provision is valid to the extent to which it does not exceed power; and
-- src:45 | (b) the remainder of the Act is not affected.
@ref s 9(2) (src:43-45)
GIVEN `the provision would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision has effect to the extent to which it does not exceed power (s 9(2)(a))` IS
    IF `the provision would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:43 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a provision of an Act would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding power—
-- src:44 | (a) the provision is valid to the extent to which it does not exceed power; and
-- src:45 | (b) the remainder of the Act is not affected.
@ref s 9(2) (src:43-45)
GIVEN `the provision would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remainder of the Act is affected (s 9(2)(b))` IS
    IF `the provision would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): if the application of a provision to a person, matter or circumstance would be interpreted as exceeding power, its application to others is not affected.
-- src:46 | (3) Without limiting subsection (1), if the application of a provision of an Act to a person, matter or circumstance would, apart from this section, be interpreted as exceeding power, the provision’s application to other persons, matters or circumstances is not affected.
@ref s 9(3) (src:46-46)
GIVEN `the application to a person, matter or circumstance would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision's application to other persons, matters or circumstances is affected (s 9(3))` IS
    IF `the application to a person, matter or circumstance would apart from s 9 be interpreted as exceeding power` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:47 | (4) This section applies to an Act in addition to, and without limiting, any provision of the Act.
@ref s 9(4) (src:47-47)
GIVEN `the thing is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 applies to an Act in addition to, and without limiting, any provision of the Act (s 9(4))` IS
    IF `the thing is an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 9A to 11 -- declaration about laws before the Australia Acts, substantive enactments, public Acts`

-- src:49 | Each provision of an Act enacted, or purporting to have been enacted, before the commencement of the Australia Acts has (and always has had) the same effect as it would have had, and is (and always has been) as valid as it would have been, if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or purported enactment.
@ref s 9A (src:49-49)
GIVEN `the provision was enacted, or purportedly enacted, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision has the same effect as it would have had, and is as valid as it would have been, if the Australia Acts had been in operation (s 9A)` IS
    IF `the provision was enacted, or purportedly enacted, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:51 | Every section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words.
@ref s 10 (src:51-51)
GIVEN `the provision is a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words (s 10)` IS
    IF `the provision is a section of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- "Every Act passed after 26 July 1852 is a public Act unless the Act otherwise expressly provides."
-- An Act passed on or before 26 July 1852 is outside the section's date, which is a scope limit with no "only": NOTHING.
-- FORK once the Act otherwise expressly provides, s 11 answers NOTHING (the Act's own provision governs) || JUST FALSE (the Act is then not a public Act)
-- src:53 | Every Act passed after 26 July 1852 is a public Act unless the Act otherwise expressly provides.
@ref s 11 (src:53-53)
GIVEN `the date the Act was passed` IS A DATE
      `the Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act is a public Act (s 11)` IS
    IF `the date the Act was passed` GREATER THAN Date 26 7 1852 AND (NOT `the Act otherwise expressly provides`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 12 and 12A -- private Acts`

DECLARE `What a private Act is said to do` IS ONE OF
    `affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person`
    `impose liabilities on the Crown or another person in relation to previous acts or omissions`
    `anything else`

-- FORK "except so far as it otherwise expressly provides" and the (2) carve-out once met: NOTHING (the section no longer answers) || JUST TRUE (the Act does the thing)
-- s 12(1): a "private Act" does not do (a) or (b), except so far as it otherwise expressly provides.
-- s 12(2): subsection (1) does not affect rights conferred, or liabilities imposed, on a person at whose instance or for whose special benefit
-- the Act is passed, or on another person claiming by, through or under such a person.
-- The question is whether the "private Act" does the thing.  Where the exception or (2) applies the section does not answer: NOTHING.
-- src:55 | (1) A private Act does not—
-- src:56 | (a) affect pre-existing rights in a way prejudicial to the Crown or another person; or
-- src:57 | (b) impose liabilities on the Crown or another person in relation to previous acts or omissions;
-- src:58 | except so far as the Act otherwise expressly provides.
@ref s 12(1) (src:55-58)
-- src:59 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect rights conferred, or liabilities imposed, on—
-- src:60 | (a) a person at whose instance, or for whose special benefit, the Act is passed; or
-- src:61 | (b) another person claiming by, through or under such a person.
@ref s 12(2) (src:59-61)
GIVEN `the Act is a private Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the Act is said to do` IS A `What a private Act is said to do`
      `the Act otherwise expressly provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right or liability concerns a person for whose special benefit the Act is passed, or a person claiming by, through or under such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a private Act does the thing (s 12)` IS
    IF NOT `the Act is a private Act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `what the Act is said to do`
        WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            IF    `the Act otherwise expressly provides`
               OR `the right or liability concerns a person for whose special benefit the Act is passed, or a person claiming by, through or under such a person`
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:63 | A private Act does not become a public Act merely because it has been amended by or under a public Act.
@ref s 12A (src:63-63)
GIVEN `the Act is a private Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been amended by or under a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a private Act has become a public Act merely because it was amended by or under a public Act (s 12A)` IS
    IF `the Act is a private Act` AND `it has been amended by or under a public Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 13, 13A and 13B -- the Crown, native title, the Legislative Assembly`

-- s 13: no Act passed after the commencement of this Act is binding on the Crown or derogates from a prerogative right unless express words are included.
-- src:65 | No Act passed after the commencement of this Act shall be binding on the Crown or derogate from any prerogative right of the Crown unless express words are included in the Act for that purpose.
@ref s 13 (src:65-65)
GIVEN `the Act was passed after the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `express words are included in the Act for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act binds the Crown or derogates from a prerogative right of the Crown (s 13)` IS
    IF `the Act was passed after the commencement of this Act` AND (NOT `express words are included in the Act for that purpose`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 13A(1): an Act enacted after the commencement of s 13A affects native title only so far as it expressly provides.
-- src:67 | (1) An Act enacted after the commencement of this section affects native title only so far as the Act expressly provides.
@ref s 13A(1) (src:67-67)
GIVEN `the Act was enacted after the commencement of s 13A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly provides that it affects native title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act affects native title (s 13A(1))` IS
    IF `the Act was enacted after the commencement of s 13A` THEN JUST `the Act expressly provides that it affects native title` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 13A(2): for (1), an Act affects native title if it extinguishes the rights and interests, or is wholly or partly inconsistent with their continued existence, enjoyment or exercise.
-- src:68 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an Act affects native title if it extinguishes the native title rights and interests or it is otherwise wholly or partly inconsistent with their continued existence, enjoyment or exercise.
@ref s 13A(2) (src:68-68)
GIVEN `the Act extinguishes the native title rights and interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act is wholly or partly inconsistent with the continued existence, enjoyment or exercise of the native title rights and interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act affects native title for s 13A(1) (s 13A(2))` IS
    JUST (   `the Act extinguishes the native title rights and interests`
          OR `the Act is wholly or partly inconsistent with the continued existence, enjoyment or exercise of the native title rights and interests`)

-- src:70 | (1) An Act enacted after the commencement of this section affects the powers, rights or immunities of the Legislative Assembly or of its members or committees only so far as the Act expressly provides.
@ref s 13B(1) (src:70-70)
GIVEN `the Act was enacted after the commencement of s 13B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly provides that it affects the powers, rights or immunities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities of the Legislative Assembly or of its members or committees (s 13B(1))` IS
    IF `the Act was enacted after the commencement of s 13B` THEN JUST `the Act expressly provides that it affects the powers, rights or immunities` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:71 | (2) For subsection (1), an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities mentioned in the subsection if it abolishes any of the powers, rights or immunities or is otherwise wholly or partly inconsistent with their continued existence, enjoyment or exercise.
@ref s 13B(2) (src:71-71)
GIVEN `the Act abolishes any of the powers, rights or immunities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act is wholly or partly inconsistent with their continued existence, enjoyment or exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act affects the powers, rights or immunities mentioned in s 13B(1) (s 13B(2))` IS
    JUST (`the Act abolishes any of the powers, rights or immunities` OR `the Act is wholly or partly inconsistent with their continued existence, enjoyment or exercise`)

-- src:72 | (3) In this section—
-- src:73 | rights includes privileges.
@ref s 13B(3) (src:72-73)
GIVEN `the thing is a privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rights in s 13B includes privileges (s 13B(3))` IS
    IF `the thing is a privilege` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14 -- Material that is, and is not, part of an Act`

DECLARE `Material in or with an Act` IS ONE OF
    `a heading to a chapter, part, division or subdivision`
    `a heading to a section, subsection or another provision`
    `an example of the operation of a provision`
    `a note to the Act or to a provision of the Act`
    `a schedule or appendix`
    `punctuation`
    `a footnote or editor's note to an Act or provision, or an endnote to an Act`

-- s 14(2): a heading to a section, subsection or another provision is part of the Act if (a) the Act is enacted after 30 June 1991, or (b) the heading is amended or inserted after 30 June 1991.
-- src:75 | (1) A heading to a chapter, part, division or subdivision of an Act is part of the Act.
@ref s 14(1) (src:75-75)
-- src:76 | (2) A heading to a section, subsection or another provision of an Act is part of the Act if—
-- src:77 | (a) the Act is enacted after 30 June 1991; or
-- src:78 | (b) the heading is amended or inserted after 30 June 1991.
@ref s 14(2) (src:76-78)
-- src:79 | (3) An example in an Act of the operation of a provision of the Act is part of the Act.
@ref s 14(3) (src:79-79)
-- src:80 | (4) A note in an Act to the Act or to a provision of the Act, as opposed to a footnote, an editor’s note or an endnote mentioned in subsection (7), is part of the Act.
-- src:81 | Example of a note—
-- src:82 | See the note to section 2.
-- src:83 | Example of a footnote—
-- src:84 | See the footnote to schedule 1, definition Acting Governor.
@ref s 14(4) (src:80-84)
-- src:85 | (5) A schedule or appendix of an Act is part of the Act.
@ref s 14(5) (src:85-85)
-- src:86 | (6) Punctuation in an Act is part of the Act.
@ref s 14(6) (src:86-86)
-- src:87 | (7) A footnote or editor’s note to an Act or to a provision of an Act, and an endnote to an Act, are not part of the Act.
@ref s 14(7) (src:87-87)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in or with an Act`
      `the date the Act was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the heading was amended or inserted after 30 June 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is part of the Act (s 14)` IS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `a heading to a chapter, part, division or subdivision` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a heading to a section, subsection or another provision` THEN
        JUST (`the date the Act was enacted` GREATER THAN Date 30 6 1991 OR `the heading was amended or inserted after 30 June 1991`)
    WHEN `an example of the operation of a provision` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a note to the Act or to a provision of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a schedule or appendix` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `punctuation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a footnote or editor's note to an Act or provision, or an endnote to an Act` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `s 14A -- Interpretation best achieving Act's purpose`

-- (1): the interpretation that will best achieve the purpose of the Act is to be preferred to any other.  Another interpretation: the section does not say.
-- src:89 | (1) In the interpretation of a provision of an Act, the interpretation that will best achieve the purpose of the Act is to be preferred to any other interpretation.
@ref s 14A(1) (src:89-89)
GIVEN `the interpretation will best achieve the purpose of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation (s 14A(1))` IS
    IF `the interpretation will best achieve the purpose of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:90 | (2) Subsection (1) does not create or extend criminal liability, but applies whether or not the Act’s purpose is expressly stated in the Act.
@ref s 14A(2) (src:90-90)
GIVEN `the purpose is expressly stated in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14A(1) applies (s 14A(2))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:90 | (2) Subsection (1) does not create or extend criminal liability, but applies whether or not the Act’s purpose is expressly stated in the Act.
@ref s 14A(2) (src:90-90)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14A(1) creates or extends criminal liability (s 14A(2))` IS FALSE

-- src:91 | (3) To remove any doubt, it is declared that this section applies to an Act passed after 30 June 1991 despite any presumption or rule of interpretation.
-- src:92 | Example—
-- src:93 | There is judicial authority for a rule of interpretation that taxing legislation is to be interpreted strictly and in a taxpayer’s favour (for example, see Partington v AG (1869) LR 4 HL 100 at 122). Despite such a possible rule, this section requires a provision imposing taxation to be interpreted in the way that best achieves the Act’s purpose, whether or not to do so would be in a taxpayer’s favour.
@ref s 14A(3) (src:91-93)
GIVEN `the date the Act was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14A applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 14A(3))` IS
    IF `the date the Act was passed` GREATER THAN Date 30 6 1991 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14B -- Use of extrinsic material in interpretation`

DECLARE `Purpose for which extrinsic material is considered` IS ONE OF
    `to provide an interpretation of a provision that is ambiguous or obscure`
    `to provide an interpretation that avoids a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable`
    `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision`

-- (1): "Subject to subsection (2), ... consideration may be given to extrinsic material capable of assisting in the interpretation"
-- (a) if ambiguous or obscure, (b) if the ordinary meaning leads to a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result, (c) in any other case.
-- A permission limited by its own "if": outside the limit the section is silent (NOTHING).
-- FORK each limb of s 14B(1) answers NOTHING when its condition is not met (a grant limited in its own wording) || JUST FALSE (the "if" condition fails)
-- src:95 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), in the interpretation of a provision of an Act, consideration may be given to extrinsic material capable of assisting in the interpretation—
-- src:96 | (a) if the provision is ambiguous or obscure—to provide an interpretation of it; or
-- src:97 | (b) if the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable—to provide an interpretation that avoids such a result; or
-- src:98 | (c) in any other case—to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision.
@ref s 14B(1) (src:95-98)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose for which extrinsic material is considered`
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consideration may be given to extrinsic material for the purpose (s 14B(1))` IS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `to provide an interpretation of a provision that is ambiguous or obscure` THEN
        IF `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `to provide an interpretation that avoids a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable` THEN
        IF `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision` THEN
        IF (NOT `the provision is ambiguous or obscure`) AND (NOT `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Matter to which regard is to be had` IS ONE OF
    `the desirability of a provision being interpreted as having its ordinary meaning`
    `the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage`
    `other relevant matters`

-- src:99 | (2) In determining whether consideration should be given to extrinsic material, and in determining the weight to be given to extrinsic material, regard is to be had to—
-- src:100 | (a) the desirability of a provision being interpreted as having its ordinary meaning; and
-- src:101 | (b) the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage; and
-- src:102 | (c) other relevant matters.
@ref s 14B(2) (src:99-102)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Matter to which regard is to be had`
DECIDE `the matters to which regard is to be had in deciding whether to consider extrinsic material and what weight to give it (s 14B(2))` IS
    LIST
        `the desirability of a provision being interpreted as having its ordinary meaning`,
        `the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage`,
        `other relevant matters`

DECLARE `Kind of extrinsic material given as an example` IS ONE OF
    `material set out in an official copy of the Act`
    `a report of a royal commission, law reform commission, commission or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, laid before the Legislative Assembly before the provision was enacted`
    `a report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly made to the Legislative Assembly before the provision was enacted`
    `a treaty or other international agreement that is mentioned in the Act`
    `an explanatory note or memorandum relating to the Bill, or any other relevant document, laid before or given to the members of the Legislative Assembly before the provision was enacted`
    `the speech made to the Legislative Assembly by the member when introducing the Bill`
    `material in an official record of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly`
    `a document declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of s 14B`
    `any other material`

-- "extrinsic material means relevant material not forming part of the Act concerned, including, for example" the eight kinds (a) to (h).
-- "Means" closes the definition, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- FORK a listed example that forms part of the Act concerned: JUST FALSE (the "means" limb governs) || JUST TRUE (the example list governs)
-- src:103 | (3) In this section—
-- src:104 | extrinsic material means relevant material not forming part of the Act concerned, including, for example—
@ref s 14B(3) (src:103-104)
GIVEN `the material is relevant to the interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material forms part of the Act concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is extrinsic material (s 14B(3))` IS
    JUST (`the material is relevant to the interpretation` AND (NOT `the material forms part of the Act concerned`))

-- src:105 | (a) material set out in an official copy of the Act; and
-- src:106 | (b) a report of a royal commission, law reform commission, commission or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, that was laid before the Legislative Assembly before the provision concerned was enacted; and
-- src:107 | (c) a report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Legislative Assembly before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:108 | (d) a treaty or other international agreement that is mentioned in the Act; and
-- src:109 | (e) an explanatory note or memorandum relating to the Bill that contained the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or given to the members of, the Legislative Assembly by the member bringing in the Bill before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:110 | (f) the speech made to the Legislative Assembly by the member when introducing the Bill; and
-- src:111 | Note—
-- src:112 | See section 53 in relation to Bills introduced before the commencement of that section.
-- src:113 | (g) material in an official record of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly; and
-- src:114 | (h) a document that is declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 14B(3) (src:105-114)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of extrinsic material given as an example`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind of material is given as an example of extrinsic material (s 14B(3)(a) to (h))` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `any other material` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:115 | ordinary meaning means the ordinary meaning conveyed by a provision having regard to its context in the Act and to the purpose of the Act.
@ref s 14B(3) (src:115-115)
GIVEN `the meaning is the one conveyed by the provision having regard to its context in the Act and to the purpose of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meaning is the ordinary meaning (s 14B(3), definition ordinary meaning)` IS
    JUST `the meaning is the one conveyed by the provision having regard to its context in the Act and to the purpose of the Act`

§§ `ss 14C to 14D -- drafting practice, general law, examples`

-- "the ideas must not be taken to be different merely because different words are used": a flat negative once both limbs hold.
-- src:117 | If—
-- src:118 | (a) a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words; and
-- src:119 | (b) a provision enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice, including, for example—
-- src:120 | (i) the use of a clearer or simpler style; or
-- src:121 | (ii) the use of gender-neutral language;
-- src:122 | the ideas must not be taken to be different merely because different words are used.
@ref s 14C (src:117-122)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different words are used (s 14C)` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act expresses an idea in particular words`
       AND `a provision enacted later appears to express the same idea in different words for the purpose of implementing a different legislative drafting practice`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:124 | (1) If—
-- src:125 | (a) a provision of an Act expressly provides for an obligation to comply with the principles of natural justice; and
-- src:126 | (b) the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for the obligation;
-- src:127 | the absence of an express provision for the obligation in the corresponding provision does not limit or otherwise affect an obligation under the corresponding provision to comply with procedural fairness implied under the general law.
@ref s 14CA(1) (src:124-127)
GIVEN `a provision expressly provides for an obligation to comply with the principles of natural justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to comply with procedural fairness implied under the general law (s 14CA(1))` IS
    IF `a provision expressly provides for an obligation to comply with the principles of natural justice`
       AND `the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for the obligation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:128 | (2) If—
-- src:129 | (a) a provision of an Act expressly provides for a function to be performed reasonably or a power to be exercised reasonably; and
-- src:130 | (b) the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for the function to be performed reasonably or the power to be exercised reasonably;
-- src:131 | the absence of an express provision for the matter in the corresponding provision does not limit or otherwise affect an obligation under the corresponding provision to perform the function reasonably or exercise the power reasonably implied under the general law.
@ref s 14CA(2) (src:128-131)
GIVEN `a provision expressly provides for a function to be performed reasonably or a power to be exercised reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence of an express provision limits or affects an obligation to perform the function or exercise the power reasonably implied under the general law (s 14CA(2))` IS
    IF `a provision expressly provides for a function to be performed reasonably or a power to be exercised reasonably`
       AND `the provision is replaced by a corresponding provision that does not expressly provide for it`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): "a provision of an Act (a former provision) is replaced by a corresponding provision if" (a), (b) or (c).  "If" without "only": NOTHING outside.
-- FORK s 14CA(3) answers NOTHING when none of (a) to (c) holds (no "only") || JUST FALSE
-- src:132 | (3) For this section, a provision of an Act (a former provision) is replaced by a corresponding provision if—
-- src:133 | (a) an amendment of the Act omits the former provision and inserts a corresponding provision, whether in the same or a different location; or
-- src:134 | (b) the former provision is amended and the amended provision is a corresponding provision; or
-- src:135 | (c) the Act is repealed by an Act that includes a corresponding provision to the former provision.
@ref s 14CA(3) (src:132-135)
GIVEN `an amendment of the Act omits the former provision and inserts a corresponding provision, whether in the same or a different location` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the former provision is amended and the amended provision is a corresponding provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act is repealed by an Act that includes a corresponding provision to the former provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a former provision is replaced by a corresponding provision (s 14CA(3))` IS
    IF    `an amendment of the Act omits the former provision and inserts a corresponding provision, whether in the same or a different location`
       OR `the former provision is amended and the amended provision is a corresponding provision`
       OR `the Act is repealed by an Act that includes a corresponding provision to the former provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:136 | (4) In this section—
-- src:137 | corresponding provision, to another provision, means a provision that is substantially the same as, or substantially equivalent to, the other provision.
@ref s 14CA(4) (src:136-137)
GIVEN `the provision is substantially the same as, or substantially equivalent to, the other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision is a corresponding provision to another provision (s 14CA(4))` IS
    JUST `the provision is substantially the same as, or substantially equivalent to, the other provision`

-- s 14D: an example is not exhaustive; does not limit but may extend the meaning; read in context; if inconsistent the provision prevails.
DECLARE `Which of an example and a provision prevails` IS ONE OF
    `the provision prevails`
    `the example prevails`

-- src:139 | If an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision—
-- src:140 | (a) the example is not exhaustive; and
-- src:141 | (b) the example does not limit, but may extend, the meaning of the provision; and
-- src:142 | (c) the example and the provision are to be read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, but, if the example and the provision so read are inconsistent, the provision prevails.
@ref s 14D (src:139-142)
GIVEN `the example and the provision, read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, are inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which of an example and a provision prevails`
DECIDE `which prevails, the example or the provision (s 14D(c))` IS
    IF `the example and the provision, read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, are inconsistent`
    THEN JUST `the provision prevails`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:139 | If an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision—
-- src:140 | (a) the example is not exhaustive; and
-- src:141 | (b) the example does not limit, but may extend, the meaning of the provision; and
-- src:142 | (c) the example and the provision are to be read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, but, if the example and the provision so read are inconsistent, the provision prevails.
@ref s 14D (src:139-142)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an example is exhaustive (s 14D(a))` IS FALSE

-- src:139 | If an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision—
-- src:140 | (a) the example is not exhaustive; and
-- src:141 | (b) the example does not limit, but may extend, the meaning of the provision; and
-- src:142 | (c) the example and the provision are to be read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, but, if the example and the provision so read are inconsistent, the provision prevails.
@ref s 14D (src:139-142)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an example limits the meaning of the provision (s 14D(b))` IS FALSE

-- src:139 | If an Act includes an example of the operation of a provision—
-- src:140 | (a) the example is not exhaustive; and
-- src:141 | (b) the example does not limit, but may extend, the meaning of the provision; and
-- src:142 | (c) the example and the provision are to be read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the Act, but, if the example and the provision so read are inconsistent, the provision prevails.
@ref s 14D (src:139-142)
GIVEN `the example extends the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an example extends the meaning of the provision (s 14D(b))` IS
    IF `the example extends the meaning of the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
